# Free Pascal / Lazarus build artifacts
lib/
*.o
*.ppu
*.rsj
*.compiled
*.res
newVMtest
newVMtest.exe
newvmconfigure
newvmconfigure.exe
newVMbench
newVMbench.exe
newVMbench_purepascal
newVMbench_purepascal.exe
newVMCLbench
newVMCLbench.exe
newVMCLfft8192bench
newVMCLfft8192bench.exe

# Third-party runtime DLLs that are sometimes copied next to the exe for
# local testing (see CLAUDE.md's Windows build notes) - not project sources
openblas.dll

# Demo project binaries: each demos/<Name>/ produces an extensionless
# binary named after its project - ignore those, keep everything with
# an extension (.pas/.lpr/.lpi/.lfm/.ico/...).
demos/*/[A-Za-z]*
!demos/*/*.*

# demos/Chebyshev/ groups its sub-projects one level deeper than the
# demos/<Name>/ layout above (e.g. demos/Chebyshev/NormalIntegration/).
# The rule above also matches the *grouping* directory itself, though -
# "NormalIntegration" looks exactly like an extensionless binary name
# from its point of view, so git excludes the whole subtree outright,
# before the "!demos/*/*.*" negation ever gets a chance to run against
# files inside it (an excluded directory isn't descended into at all).
# Un-ignore the grouping directory and its subdirectories first, then
# re-apply the same ignore-extensionless/keep-extension pattern one
# level deeper. [A-Za-z0-9] (not just [A-Za-z], unlike the demos/*/ and
# Graphs/*/ rules above) since demos/Chebyshev/2DChebBVP_FPC/'s binary
# is named "2DChebBVP" - starting with a digit - which the letter-only
# class silently failed to match, leaving that binary untracked instead
# of ignored.
!demos/Chebyshev/
!demos/Chebyshev/*/
demos/Chebyshev/*/[A-Za-z0-9]*
!demos/Chebyshev/*/*.*

# Same for Graphs/<Name>/ (Plot2D, Plot3D) - unlike demos/, these are only
# ignored on Linux where the binary has no extension; Windows .exe builds
# are caught by the unscoped *.exe rule below either way.
Graphs/*/[A-Za-z]*
!Graphs/*/*.*

# SDR_Radio is its own top-level project directory (one level shallower
# than demos/<Name>/ or Graphs/<Name>/, so no /*/ here) - same
# ignore-extensionless-binary/keep-extension pattern as those two.
SDR_Radio/[A-Za-z]*
!SDR_Radio/*.*

# Windows demo binaries do have an extension (.exe), so the negations above
# re-include them - this rule comes after those negations (later patterns
# win) to actually exclude them, e.g. demos/SpectralDiff/SpectralDiff.exe.
# Same story for lazbuild's own *.compiled state file (already ignored
# unscoped near the top of this file) - it has a dot too, so it needs
# repeating here for the same reason, e.g. Graphs/Plot2D/Plot2D.compiled.
*.exe
*.compiled

# Delphi/RAD Studio build artifacts and IDE-local state - demos/Chebyshev/
# ChebBVP and demos/Chebyshev/Normal_Integration keep the original Delphi/
# MtxVec sources these were ported from (see uCheb.pas/uBVPMain.pas's own
# header comments for the newVM/FPC recodings), but not RAD Studio's own
# compiled output or per-machine IDE state - same principle as the
# Lazarus artifacts ignored above. Re-states *.res (already ignored
# unscoped near the top of this file) since the "!demos/Chebyshev/*/*.*"
# negation above would otherwise re-include it for anything under
# demos/Chebyshev/ specifically - later patterns win, so it has to be
# repeated here rather than relying on the earlier occurrence.
*.res
*.dcu
*.rsm
*.dproj.local
*.identcache
*.stat
*.dsk
*.~dsk
__history/
Win64/

# Lazarus IDE session state (per-user, not shared project config)
*.lps
Graphs/packagefiles.xml

# macOS Finder metadata, and dSYM debug-symbol bundles fpc/ld leave next to
# a Darwin binary (e.g. demos/FunctionPlot/FunctionPlot.dSYM/) - the latter
# has a dot in its name, so it isn't caught by the demos/*/[A-Za-z]* rule
# above (the "!demos/*/*.*" negation re-includes anything with an
# extension-shaped name); this comes after that negation so it wins.
.DS_Store
*.dSYM/

# Claude Code local settings
.claude/settings.local.json
